From: piano bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] BootShim: describe the whole image in the ARM64 header

Upstream writes FD_SIZE into the ARM64 image_size field, which is only the
firmware volume length and omits the shim bytes that precede it. UniXNU's
bootimg step rejects such an image ("the ARM64 image header does not describe
the shim plus the firmware volume"); the marble port fixed the same thing the
same way. The expression resolves at assembly time, so the header keeps the
exact value len(shim) + FD_SIZE.

--- a/BootShim/BootShim.S
+++ b/BootShim/BootShim.S
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ _StackBase:
   .quad FD_BASE         /* Text Offset */
 
 _StackSize:
-  .quad FD_SIZE         /* Image Size */
+  .quad FD_SIZE + _Payload - _Head   /* Image Size */
   .quad 0               /* Flags */
   .quad 0               /* Reserved */
   .quad 0               /* Reserved */
